    "title": "EFD hosts hands-on vehicle fire training - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nHENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — The Evansville Fire Department spent the day setting things on fire, but for a good reason.\nNew recruits got some hands-on experience setting controlled car fires and learning how to put them out. The training also helped investigators study burn patterns to better determine a fire’s cause.\nK9 Indie was also at the training. Fire officials say K9 units can detect specific scents and alert crews to possible evidence.\nWe’re told the samples are then sent-off for testing helping investigators figure out what sparked a fire.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "New recruits got some hands-on experience setting controlled car fires and learning how to put them out. The training also helped investigators study burn patterns to better determine a fire’s cause. Fire officials say K9 units can detect specific scents and alert crews to possible evidence. We’re told the samples are then sent-off for testing helping investigators figure out what sparked a fire. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
